{"componentChunkName":"component---src-templates-post-js","path":"/posts/feature-flagging-gemini-features-in-angular-with-ngx-feature-toggle/","result":{"data":{"markdownRemark":{"html":"<p><span\n      class=\"gatsby-resp-image-wrapper\"\n      style=\"position: relative; display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; max-width: 1280px; \"\n    >\n      <a\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-link\"\n    href=\"/static/e518e3a029afb3eacb314800f3751d5d/00711/hero.png\"\n    style=\"display: block\"\n    target=\"_blank\"\n    rel=\"noopener\"\n  >\n    <span\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-background-image\"\n    style=\"padding-bottom: 33.4375%; position: relative; bottom: 0; left: 0; background-image: url('data:image/png;base64,'); background-size: cover; display: block;\"\n  ></span>\n  <picture>\n          <source\n              srcset=\"/static/e518e3a029afb3eacb314800f3751d5d/fb34c/hero.avif 320w,\n/static/e518e3a029afb3eacb314800f3751d5d/646cd/hero.avif 768w,\n/static/e518e3a029afb3eacb314800f3751d5d/8b485/hero.avif 1024w,\n/static/e518e3a029afb3eacb314800f3751d5d/a73d6/hero.avif 1280w,\n/static/e518e3a029afb3eacb314800f3751d5d/a7f9f/hero.avif 1920w,\n/static/e518e3a029afb3eacb314800f3751d5d/fb732/hero.avif 2400w\"\n              sizes=\"(max-width: 1280px) 100vw, 1280px\"\n              type=\"image/avif\"\n            /><source\n              srcset=\"/static/e518e3a029afb3eacb314800f3751d5d/cb523/hero.webp 320w,\n/static/e518e3a029afb3eacb314800f3751d5d/cd067/hero.webp 768w,\n/static/e518e3a029afb3eacb314800f3751d5d/53334/hero.webp 1024w,\n/static/e518e3a029afb3eacb314800f3751d5d/4b075/hero.webp 1280w,\n/static/e518e3a029afb3eacb314800f3751d5d/f3ff0/hero.webp 1920w,\n/static/e518e3a029afb3eacb314800f3751d5d/4293a/hero.webp 2400w\"\n              sizes=\"(max-width: 1280px) 100vw, 1280px\"\n              type=\"image/webp\"\n            />\n          <source\n            srcset=\"/static/e518e3a029afb3eacb314800f3751d5d/d4f27/hero.png 320w,\n/static/e518e3a029afb3eacb314800f3751d5d/778aa/hero.png 768w,\n/static/e518e3a029afb3eacb314800f3751d5d/658fc/hero.png 1024w,\n/static/e518e3a029afb3eacb314800f3751d5d/26c69/hero.png 1280w,\n/static/e518e3a029afb3eacb314800f3751d5d/7d442/hero.png 1920w,\n/static/e518e3a029afb3eacb314800f3751d5d/00711/hero.png 2400w\"\n            sizes=\"(max-width: 1280px) 100vw, 1280px\"\n            type=\"image/png\"\n          />\n          <img\n            class=\"gatsby-resp-image-image\"\n            src=\"/static/e518e3a029afb3eacb314800f3751d5d/26c69/hero.png\"\n            alt=\"hero\"\n            title=\"\"\n            loading=\"lazy\"\n            decoding=\"async\"\n            style=\"width:100%;height:100%;margin:0;vertical-align:middle;position:absolute;top:0;left:0;\"\n          />\n        </picture>\n  </a>\n    </span></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>TL;DR; Treat every AI feature as a release you can turn off. Put it behind <code class=\"language-text\">*featureToggle</code>, guard its routes with <code class=\"language-text\">featureToggleGuard</code>, flip it at runtime with <code class=\"language-text\">FeatureToggleService</code>, and always render something useful when the model is not available 🎉</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Introduction</h3>\n<p>If 2026 taught me one thing about AI features on the web, it is that they fail in more ways than a regular feature. The model can be slow, expensive, wrong, or simply not on the device yet. Built-in AI in Chrome, like the <a href=\"https://developer.chrome.com/docs/ai/summarizer-api\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">Summarizer API</a> running Gemini Nano, downloads the model on first use, and some devices will never meet the hardware requirements. Cloud models have quotas and bills.</p>\n<p>None of that is a reason to avoid shipping. It is a reason to ship with a switch in your hand.</p>\n<p>In this article, we'll explore how to put a Gemini-powered \"Summarize\" button behind a feature toggle in Angular using <a href=\"https://github.com/willmendesneto/ngx-feature-toggle\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">ngx-feature-toggle</a>, roll it out gradually, keep a kill switch, and render a fallback UI when the model is unavailable. If you want the background on the library itself, I wrote about it in <a href=\"/posts/ngx-feature-toggle-flexible-user-management-and-page-access-control-for-angular-apps/\">NGX-Feature-Toggle — Flexible User Management and Page Access control</a>.</p>\n<h2>The Problem with shipping AI features \"always on\"</h2>\n<p>Picture a summary button on an article page. It works on your machine. Then it reaches production and:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>some users see a button that does nothing, because their device can't run the on-device model;</li>\n<li>a prompt change makes the output worse, and you need a full deploy to roll it back;</li>\n<li>cloud usage grows faster than the budget, and the only lever is a hotfix;</li>\n<li>a new \"AI lab\" page is reachable by URL before it's ready.</li>\n</ul>\n<blockquote>\n<p>An AI feature without a kill switch is an incident waiting for a deploy window.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h2>The Solution: toggles in templates, routes and at runtime</h2>\n<p>The latest <code class=\"language-text\">ngx-feature-toggle</code> (v13 at the time of writing) is built around standalone APIs and signals, and it requires Angular 22 or newer. Older apps can keep using the previous major versions.</p>\n<h4>1. Safe defaults at bootstrap</h4>\n<p>Start with every AI flag <strong>off</strong>. If the remote configuration never arrives, users get the classic experience instead of a broken one.</p>\n<div class=\"gatsby-highlight\" data-language=\"typescript\"><pre class=\"language-typescript\"><code class=\"language-typescript\"><span class=\"token comment\">// app.config.ts</span>\n<span class=\"token keyword\">import</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span> ApplicationConfig<span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span> inject<span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span> provideAppInitializer <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">from</span> <span class=\"token string\">'@angular/core'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n<span class=\"token keyword\">import</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span> provideRouter <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">from</span> <span class=\"token string\">'@angular/router'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n<span class=\"token keyword\">import</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span> FeatureToggleService<span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span> provideFeatureToggles <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">from</span> <span class=\"token string\">'ngx-feature-toggle'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n<span class=\"token keyword\">import</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span> routes <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">from</span> <span class=\"token string\">'./app.routes'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n\n<span class=\"token keyword\">export</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">const</span> appConfig<span class=\"token operator\">:</span> ApplicationConfig <span class=\"token operator\">=</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n  providers<span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">[</span>\n    <span class=\"token function\">provideRouter</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span>routes<span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n    <span class=\"token function\">provideFeatureToggles</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n      enableAiSummary<span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token boolean\">false</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n      enableAiLab<span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token boolean\">false</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n      aiKillSwitch<span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token boolean\">false</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n    <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n    <span class=\"token function\">provideAppInitializer</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token keyword\">async</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span> <span class=\"token operator\">=></span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n      <span class=\"token keyword\">const</span> toggles <span class=\"token operator\">=</span> <span class=\"token function\">inject</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span>FeatureToggleService<span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n      <span class=\"token keyword\">try</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n        <span class=\"token keyword\">const</span> response <span class=\"token operator\">=</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">await</span> <span class=\"token function\">fetch</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token string\">'/api/feature-toggles'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n        <span class=\"token keyword\">if</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span>response<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span>ok<span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n          toggles<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span><span class=\"token function\">set</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token keyword\">await</span> response<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span><span class=\"token function\">json</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n        <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span>\n      <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">catch</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n        <span class=\"token comment\">// Network error: keep the safe defaults, AI features stay off.</span>\n      <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span>\n    <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n  <span class=\"token punctuation\">]</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n<span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span></code></pre></div>\n<p>As you can see, <code class=\"language-text\">FeatureToggleService.set()</code> merges the values coming from the server with the defaults. The gradual rollout lives on the server: it decides, per user or per percentage bucket, whether <code class=\"language-text\">enableAiSummary</code> is <code class=\"language-text\">true</code>. The frontend only consumes booleans, which keeps the rollout logic in one place.</p>\n<h4>2. The template: feature, kill switch and fallback</h4>\n<p><code class=\"language-text\">*featureToggle</code> accepts a single name, a <code class=\"language-text\">!</code> prefix for negation, or an array where <strong>all</strong> entries must match. That array is a nice fit for a kill switch:</p>\n<div class=\"gatsby-highlight\" data-language=\"typescript\"><pre class=\"language-typescript\"><code class=\"language-typescript\"><span class=\"token keyword\">import</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span> Component<span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span> input <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">from</span> <span class=\"token string\">'@angular/core'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n<span class=\"token keyword\">import</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span> FeatureToggleDirective <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">from</span> <span class=\"token string\">'ngx-feature-toggle'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n<span class=\"token keyword\">import</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span> AiSummaryComponent <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">from</span> <span class=\"token string\">'./ai-summary.component'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n\n<span class=\"token decorator\"><span class=\"token at operator\">@</span><span class=\"token function\">Component</span></span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n  selector<span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token string\">'app-article'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n  imports<span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">[</span>FeatureToggleDirective<span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span> AiSummaryComponent<span class=\"token punctuation\">]</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n  template<span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token template-string\"><span class=\"token template-punctuation string\">`</span><span class=\"token string\">\n    &lt;ng-container *featureToggle=\"['enableAiSummary', '!aiKillSwitch']\">\n      &lt;app-ai-summary [text]=\"body()\" />\n    &lt;/ng-container>\n    &lt;ng-container *featureToggle=\"'aiKillSwitch'\">\n      &lt;p>Summaries are paused for now. The full article is below.&lt;/p>\n    &lt;/ng-container>\n    &lt;article [innerHTML]=\"body()\">&lt;/article>\n  </span><span class=\"token template-punctuation string\">`</span></span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n<span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span>\n<span class=\"token keyword\">export</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">class</span> <span class=\"token class-name\">ArticleComponent</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n  <span class=\"token keyword\">readonly</span> body <span class=\"token operator\">=</span> input<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span><span class=\"token generic-function\"><span class=\"token function\">required</span><span class=\"token generic class-name\"><span class=\"token operator\">&lt;</span><span class=\"token builtin\">string</span><span class=\"token operator\">></span></span></span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n<span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span></code></pre></div>\n<p>The kill switch is a separate flag on purpose. <code class=\"language-text\">enableAiSummary</code> describes the rollout, while <code class=\"language-text\">aiKillSwitch</code> describes an incident. When you turn the incident off, the rollout state is still there.</p>\n<h4>3. Flip it at runtime</h4>\n<p><code class=\"language-text\">FeatureToggleService</code> exposes the toggles as a signal, and every <code class=\"language-text\">*featureToggle</code> updates when they change, also in <code class=\"language-text\">OnPush</code> and zoneless apps. So that, a kill switch can arrive through Server-Sent Events, without a reload:</p>\n<div class=\"gatsby-highlight\" data-language=\"typescript\"><pre class=\"language-typescript\"><code class=\"language-typescript\"><span class=\"token keyword\">import</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span> Injectable<span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span> inject <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">from</span> <span class=\"token string\">'@angular/core'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n<span class=\"token keyword\">import</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span> FeatureToggleService <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">from</span> <span class=\"token string\">'ngx-feature-toggle'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n\n<span class=\"token decorator\"><span class=\"token at operator\">@</span><span class=\"token function\">Injectable</span></span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span> providedIn<span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token string\">'root'</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span>\n<span class=\"token keyword\">export</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">class</span> <span class=\"token class-name\">FeatureToggleStream</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n  <span class=\"token keyword\">private</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">readonly</span> toggles <span class=\"token operator\">=</span> <span class=\"token function\">inject</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span>FeatureToggleService<span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n\n  <span class=\"token function\">connect</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n    <span class=\"token keyword\">const</span> events <span class=\"token operator\">=</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">new</span> <span class=\"token class-name\">EventSource</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token string\">'/api/feature-toggles/stream'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n    events<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span><span class=\"token function-variable function\">onmessage</span> <span class=\"token operator\">=</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span>event<span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span> <span class=\"token operator\">=></span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n      <span class=\"token keyword\">try</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n        <span class=\"token keyword\">this</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span>toggles<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span><span class=\"token function\">set</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token constant\">JSON</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span><span class=\"token function\">parse</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span>event<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span>data<span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n      <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">catch</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n        <span class=\"token comment\">// Ignore malformed messages and keep the current toggles.</span>\n      <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span>\n    <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n    events<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span><span class=\"token function-variable function\">onerror</span> <span class=\"token operator\">=</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span> <span class=\"token operator\">=></span> events<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span><span class=\"token function\">close</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n  <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span>\n<span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span></code></pre></div>\n<h4>4. Guard the routes</h4>\n<p>For a whole page, like an experimental \"AI lab\", use <code class=\"language-text\">featureToggleGuard</code> with <code class=\"language-text\">canMatch</code>. The route data takes the same string, array or callback syntax, and <code class=\"language-text\">redirectTo</code> sends users somewhere useful:</p>\n<div class=\"gatsby-highlight\" data-language=\"typescript\"><pre class=\"language-typescript\"><code class=\"language-typescript\"><span class=\"token keyword\">import</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span> Routes <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">from</span> <span class=\"token string\">'@angular/router'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n<span class=\"token keyword\">import</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span> featureToggleGuard <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">from</span> <span class=\"token string\">'ngx-feature-toggle'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n\n<span class=\"token keyword\">export</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">const</span> routes<span class=\"token operator\">:</span> Routes <span class=\"token operator\">=</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">[</span>\n  <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n    path<span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token string\">'ai-lab'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n    <span class=\"token function-variable function\">loadComponent</span><span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span> <span class=\"token operator\">=></span> <span class=\"token keyword\">import</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token string\">'./ai-lab/ai-lab.component'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span><span class=\"token function\">then</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span>m<span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span> <span class=\"token operator\">=></span> m<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span>AiLabComponent<span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n    canMatch<span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">[</span>featureToggleGuard<span class=\"token punctuation\">]</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n    data<span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n      featureToggle<span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">[</span><span class=\"token string\">'enableAiLab'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span> <span class=\"token string\">'!aiKillSwitch'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">]</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n      redirectTo<span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token string\">'/'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n    <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n  <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n<span class=\"token punctuation\">]</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span></code></pre></div>\n<h4>5. A flag is not a capability check</h4>\n<p>Keep in mind: the flag says \"you <em>may</em> show this\". It doesn't say \"this device <em>can</em> run it\". The component behind the flag still checks the model. With the Summarizer API, <code class=\"language-text\">availability()</code> returns <code class=\"language-text\">\"unavailable\"</code>, <code class=\"language-text\">\"downloadable\"</code>, <code class=\"language-text\">\"downloading\"</code> or <code class=\"language-text\">\"available\"</code>, and the <a href=\"https://developer.chrome.com/docs/ai/inform-users-of-model-download\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">Chrome docs</a> recommend showing download progress for the middle two.</p>\n<div class=\"gatsby-highlight\" data-language=\"typescript\"><pre class=\"language-typescript\"><code class=\"language-typescript\"><span class=\"token keyword\">import</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span> Component<span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span> input<span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span> signal <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">from</span> <span class=\"token string\">'@angular/core'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n<span class=\"token comment\">// Typings: npm install -D @types/dom-chromium-ai</span>\n\n<span class=\"token keyword\">type</span> <span class=\"token class-name\">SummaryState</span> <span class=\"token operator\">=</span> <span class=\"token string\">'idle'</span> <span class=\"token operator\">|</span> <span class=\"token string\">'downloading'</span> <span class=\"token operator\">|</span> <span class=\"token string\">'ready'</span> <span class=\"token operator\">|</span> <span class=\"token string\">'unavailable'</span> <span class=\"token operator\">|</span> <span class=\"token string\">'error'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n\n<span class=\"token decorator\"><span class=\"token at operator\">@</span><span class=\"token function\">Component</span></span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n  selector<span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token string\">'app-ai-summary'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n  template<span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token template-string\"><span class=\"token template-punctuation string\">`</span><span class=\"token string\">\n    @switch (state()) {\n      @case ('unavailable') {\n        &lt;a href=\"#key-points\">Jump to the key points&lt;/a>\n      }\n      @case ('downloading') {\n        &lt;p>Preparing the on-device model… {{ progress() }}%&lt;/p>\n      }\n      @case ('error') {\n        &lt;p>We couldn't summarize this article. The full text is below.&lt;/p>\n      }\n      @default {\n        &lt;button type=\"button\" (click)=\"summarize()\">Summarize&lt;/button>\n        &lt;p>{{ summary() }}&lt;/p>\n      }\n    }\n  </span><span class=\"token template-punctuation string\">`</span></span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n<span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span>\n<span class=\"token keyword\">export</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">class</span> <span class=\"token class-name\">AiSummaryComponent</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n  <span class=\"token keyword\">readonly</span> text <span class=\"token operator\">=</span> input<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span><span class=\"token generic-function\"><span class=\"token function\">required</span><span class=\"token generic class-name\"><span class=\"token operator\">&lt;</span><span class=\"token builtin\">string</span><span class=\"token operator\">></span></span></span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n  <span class=\"token keyword\">readonly</span> state <span class=\"token operator\">=</span> <span class=\"token generic-function\"><span class=\"token function\">signal</span><span class=\"token generic class-name\"><span class=\"token operator\">&lt;</span>SummaryState<span class=\"token operator\">></span></span></span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token string\">'idle'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n  <span class=\"token keyword\">readonly</span> progress <span class=\"token operator\">=</span> <span class=\"token function\">signal</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token number\">0</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n  <span class=\"token keyword\">readonly</span> summary <span class=\"token operator\">=</span> <span class=\"token function\">signal</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token string\">''</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n\n  <span class=\"token keyword\">async</span> <span class=\"token function\">summarize</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n    <span class=\"token keyword\">const</span> availability <span class=\"token operator\">=</span> <span class=\"token string\">'Summarizer'</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">in</span> self <span class=\"token operator\">?</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">await</span> Summarizer<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span><span class=\"token function\">availability</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span> <span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token string\">'unavailable'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"token keyword\">if</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span>availability <span class=\"token operator\">===</span> <span class=\"token string\">'unavailable'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n      <span class=\"token keyword\">this</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span>state<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span><span class=\"token function\">set</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token string\">'unavailable'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n      <span class=\"token keyword\">return</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span>\n    <span class=\"token keyword\">try</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n      <span class=\"token keyword\">if</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span>availability <span class=\"token operator\">!==</span> <span class=\"token string\">'available'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">this</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span>state<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span><span class=\"token function\">set</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token string\">'downloading'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n      <span class=\"token keyword\">const</span> summarizer <span class=\"token operator\">=</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">await</span> Summarizer<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span><span class=\"token function\">create</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n        type<span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token string\">'tldr'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n        <span class=\"token function-variable function\">monitor</span><span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span>m<span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span> <span class=\"token operator\">=></span>\n          m<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span><span class=\"token function\">addEventListener</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token string\">'downloadprogress'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span>e<span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span> <span class=\"token operator\">=></span> <span class=\"token keyword\">this</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span>progress<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span><span class=\"token function\">set</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span>Math<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span><span class=\"token function\">round</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span>e<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span>loaded <span class=\"token operator\">*</span> <span class=\"token number\">100</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n      <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n      <span class=\"token keyword\">this</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span>state<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span><span class=\"token function\">set</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token string\">'ready'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n      <span class=\"token keyword\">this</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span>summary<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span><span class=\"token function\">set</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token keyword\">await</span> summarizer<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span><span class=\"token function\">summarize</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token keyword\">this</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span><span class=\"token function\">text</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">catch</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n      <span class=\"token keyword\">this</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span>state<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span><span class=\"token function\">set</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token string\">'error'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span>\n  <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span>\n<span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span></code></pre></div>\n<p><code class=\"language-text\">Summarizer.create()</code> runs inside the click handler because the model download needs user activation. The same shape works for a cloud fallback: swap the <code class=\"language-text\">'unavailable'</code> branch for a call to your Gemini backend, and give that call its own flag so you can turn off the paid path without touching the free on-device one.</p>\n<h3>What this gives you</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Gradual rollout</strong> decided on the server and consumed as booleans.</li>\n<li><strong>A kill switch</strong> that reaches open tabs without a deploy.</li>\n<li><strong>Fallback UI</strong> for devices that can't run the model, and for errors.</li>\n<li><strong>Routes</strong> that stay closed until the feature is ready.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>And, like any release toggle, plan its removal. Once the feature is stable, delete the flag and the dead branch. I wrote about <a href=\"/posts/automating-launchdarkly-feature-flags-cleanup-in-your-codebase/\">automating that cleanup</a> a while ago, and the advice still holds.</p>\n<p>If you're streaming the response instead of waiting for the whole summary, take a look at <a href=\"/posts/streaming-gemini-responses-into-angular-signals/\">Streaming Gemini responses into Angular signals</a> and <a href=\"/posts/skeleton-loaders-for-llm-latency-ngx-skeleton-loader-for-streaming-uis/\">Skeleton loaders for LLM latency</a> in this series.</p>\n<h2>References</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/willmendesneto/ngx-feature-toggle\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">ngx-feature-toggle on GitHub</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://www.npmjs.com/package/ngx-feature-toggle\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">ngx-feature-toggle on npm</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://developer.chrome.com/docs/ai/summarizer-api\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">Summarize with built-in AI (Summarizer API)</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://developer.chrome.com/docs/ai/inform-users-of-model-download\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">Inform users of model download</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://angular.dev/guide/routing/route-guards\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">Route guards on angular.dev</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://martinfowler.com/bliki/FeatureToggle.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">Feature Toggles, by Martin Fowler</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3>That’s all for now</h3>\n<p>Ship the AI feature, but ship the switch first.</p>\n<p>I hope you enjoyed this reading as much as I enjoyed writing it. Thank you so much for reading until the end and see you soon!</p>\n<p>🚀🚀🚀🚀🚀🚀</p>\n<hr />\n<h3>Cya 👋</h3>","frontmatter":{"date":"November 23, 2026","path":"/posts/feature-flagging-gemini-features-in-angular-with-ngx-feature-toggle/","title":"Feature flagging Gemini features in Angular with ngx-feature-toggle","tags":["ai","angular","feature-flags","gemini","frontend","architecture"],"status":"active"},"timeToRead":5}},"pageContext":{"postPath":"/posts/feature-flagging-gemini-features-in-angular-with-ngx-feature-toggle/"}},"staticQueryHashes":["1271460761","63159454"],"slicesMap":{}}